Missing: a CU that starts including a header on disk is not found from the header

a.c is rewritten on disk to include h.h and call f. A push on f in h.h then
lists only h.h and b.c. The siblings of h.h are found through the include
references in the table, and a.c has none for h.h: the scan ran on the first
request only, when a.c had no include, and a.c was never parsed.

The likely fix is that a changed file is rescanned for its includes as part of
the removal, and that the edges get a reference type that the removal leaves
alone. Decide first what the parse writes and which writer wins (include-edges,
#42). See doc/docs/20-insights.adoc, "The include edges are inputs, not
knowledge".
